@page "/technical-overview"

<PageTitle>Technical Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / WEEK 3 PRODUCTION FOUNDATION"
          Title="Technical Overview"
          Subtitle="OperationsFlow is a Blazor business workflow prototype with SQL-backed local authentication, provider-independent evidence storage, document traceability, data quality checks, and a Week 4 path toward Microsoft OAuth2 and Microsoft 365 integration."
          BadgeText="Auth + Storage Ready"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-success">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/portfolio">Portfolio Hub</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/integration-overview">Integration Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/user-roles">User Roles</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="🧩">
    <p>
        This page explains the current Week 3 architecture. The app now proves both a local/free deployment path and a Microsoft 365 production path:
        local SQL users/roles/password login for traditional internal business apps, and provider-ready storage/auth design for Week 4 Microsoft integration.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Frontend"
                Value="Blazor"
                Detail="Razor pages, reusable components, route guard, and protected navigation."
                Icon="💻"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Database"
                Value="SQL-backed"
                Detail="Workflow records, users, roles, permissions, logs, and attachment metadata."
                Icon="🗄️"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Auth Layer"
                Value="Local Login"
                Detail="Password login with persistent local session and role reload."
                Icon="🔐"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Week 4 Target"
                Value="OAuth2 + SharePoint"
                Detail="Microsoft login and Graph-backed evidence storage."
                Icon="☁️"
                Tone="warning" />
</MetricGrid>

<InfoPanel Title="Current Week 3 architecture"
           Subtitle="The local/free version now works as a more complete business-system foundation."
           Tone="default">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">UI</span>
            <h3>Shared Blazor pages</h3>
            <p>
                Registers, detail pages, reports, data quality, document library, activity log, and reviewer pages use the same internal dashboard style.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Identity</span>
            <h3>Local SQL authentication</h3>
            <p>
                LocalUsers, LocalRoles, LocalUserRoles, LocalPermissions, and LocalRolePermissions support the Week 3 local login model.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Evidence</span>
            <h3>Provider-ready attachments</h3>
            <p>
                RecordAttachments uses metadata and a storage provider interface so local storage can become SharePoint later.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Traceability</span>
            <h3>Activity Log</h3>
            <p>
                Workflow events and evidence actions are recorded for reviewer/audit visibility.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<TableCard Title="Architecture layers"
           Subtitle="The current local implementation maps directly to the Week 4 production path.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Layer</th>
                <th>Current Implementation</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">UI</span></td>
                <td>Blazor Razor pages and shared workflow components</td>
                <td>Registers, detail pages, dashboards, reports, data quality, login, and portfolio review pages.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Authentication</span></td>
                <td>Local SQL users and password login</td>
                <td>Allows the Week 3 local/free app to require login without Microsoft licensing.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Authorization</span></td>
                <td>Local roles and permission matrix</td>
                <td>Defines Admin, Manager, Reviewer, Worker, and ReadOnly app permissions.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Session</span></td>
                <td>Saved local user id with SQL reload</td>
                <td>Refresh keeps the user signed in while roles/permissions remain database-backed.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">External login prep</span></td>
                <td>ExternalLoginLinks table</td>
                <td>Prepares Week 4 Microsoft OAuth2 account linking to LocalUser records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Record evidence</span></td>
                <td>RecordAttachments component</td>
                <td>Reusable upload, view, download, and soft-delete panel for module record details.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Attachment metadata</span></td>
                <td>DocumentAttachment model and service layer</td>
                <td>Stores provider, record type, record id, file name, path/key, upload date, deletion state, and audit metadata.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Physical file storage</span></td>
                <td>Local upload provider</td>
                <td>Stores demo files under wwwroot/uploads for local proof only.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Library</span></td>
                <td>Document Library page</td>
                <td>Shows active attachment metadata across Work Orders, Corrective Actions, and Document Intake.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Traceability</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log</td>
                <td>Records upload/delete actions and workflow changes for reviewer and audit evidence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Quality</span></td>
                <td>Data Quality evidence checks</td>
                <td>Flags important records that need evidence but have no attached files.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Reporting</span></td>
                <td>Reports evidence coverage</td>
                <td>Summarises attached files, missing evidence, and module-level evidence coverage.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Local/free provider behaviour"
               Subtitle="The current provider proves the workflow without Microsoft licensing."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Login provider:</strong>
                <span>Local SQL username/password.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Authorization:</strong>
                <span>Local SQL roles and permissions.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Session:</strong>
                <span>Persistent local user id, then SQL role reload.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>File provider:</strong>
                <span>Local storage under wwwroot/uploads.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Metadata:</strong>
                <span>DocumentAttachment rows remain structured in the app database.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 production target"
               Subtitle="The production version should replace providers, not rebuild workflow pages."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Login provider:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft OAuth2 / Entra ID.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Account mapping:</strong>
                <span>Microsoft account links to LocalUser through ExternalLoginLinks.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Authorization:</strong>
                <span>Local SQL roles remain the app permission source.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>File provider:</strong>
                <span>SharePoint document library through Microsoft Graph.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Production layer:</strong>
                <span>Tenant config, secrets, HTTPS, deployment, backup, and retention.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<InfoPanel Title="Provider-independent workflow"
           Subtitle="This is the key Week 3 architecture win: the business workflow does not need to be rebuilt for Week 4."
           Tone="info">

    <div class="of-link-row">
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Login</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">LocalUser</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Roles/Permissions</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Record detail page</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">RecordAttachments</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Storage provider</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Activity Log</span>
    </div>

    <p class="of-muted-text">
        Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Document Library, Data Quality, Reports, and Activity Log should not be rebuilt for Week 4.
        Week 4 should replace the authentication and storage providers underneath the existing workflow.
    </p>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Production boundary" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
    <p>
        Week 3 proves the local/free version and production-shaped architecture. Week 4 is still needed for real Microsoft OAuth2,
        SharePoint/Graph storage, production secrets, tenant setup, hosted deployment, backup/restore, retention, and compliance hardening.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>